              <li>Limited template selection (you describe what you want)</li>
              <li>CMS add-on costs extra if you want to edit yourself</li>
              <li>Smaller company with fewer resources than Wix/Squarespace</li>
              <li>Not suitable for non-real-estate businesses</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="color:#818cf8;font-weight:600;">
          Pricing: Starter Website $499 · Professional Website $999 · Premium Website $1,999 · CMS Add-on $130 · AI Agent support $49/month (optional)
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Review: Wix -->
      <div id="wix" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:16px;">
        <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">Wix</h3>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Wix is the most popular DIY website builder with over 900 templates and a drag-and-drop editor that lets anyone build a website. Their pricing starts at $17/month (Light plan, billed annually) and goes up to $160/month (Business Elite). All plans include hosting, SSL, and a free domain for the first year on annual plans. Wix also offers AI website builder tools that can generate a basic site from a prompt.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Wix's strength is flexibility — you can build almost any type of website, from ecommerce stores to portfolios to blogs. For real estate agents, Wix has real estate templates and can integrate with IDX plugins (at an additional cost). The trade-off is that you're responsible for everything: design, layout, SEO, mobile responsiveness, content, and ongoing maintenance. A professional-looking Wix site typically takes 20-60 hours to build, and the real cost isn't the subscription — it's your time.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">✅ Pros</p>
            <ul style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
              <li>900+ templates for every industry</li>
              <li>Full drag-and-drop control over every element</li>
              <li>AI builder can generate a site in minutes</li>
              <li>App market with 300+ integrations</li>
              <li>Free domain (first year on annual plans)</li>
              <li>Built-in SEO tools and analytics</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">⚠️ Cons</p>
            <ul style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
              <li>20-60 hours of your time to build a professional site</li>
              <li>Recurring subscription costs forever</li>
              <li>No native IDX/MLS integration — requires third-party plugins</li>
              <li>No AI lead capture or receptionist built in</li>
              <li>Not designed specifically for real estate</li>
              <li>SEO mistakes are easy to make if you're not experienced</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="color:#818cf8;font-weight:600;">
          Pricing: Light $17/mo · Core $30/mo · Business $40/mo · Business Elite $160/mo (all billed annually)
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Review: Squarespace -->
      <div id="squarespace" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <h3 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">Squarespace</h3>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Squarespace is known for its beautiful, design-forward templates. It's slightly less flexible than Wix but produces consistently polished results. Pricing starts at $16/month (Personal plan, billed annually) and goes up to $99/month (Advanced plan). All plans include hosting, SSL, 24/7 support, and a free domain for the first year on annual plans. Squarespace also offers AI-powered design tools for faster setup.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          Squarespace's templates are generally better-looking out of the box than Wix's, but they're harder to customize. The editor is clean but constraining — you work within the template's structure rather than placing elements freely. For real estate agents, Squarespace has real estate templates and can integrate with IDX services, but it requires more technical know-how than Wix to set up properly. Like Wix, the real cost is the 20-60 hours of your time to build and optimize.
        </p>
